8</volume><fpage>1525</fpage><lpage>1529</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2166087</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000503-deJong1"><label>10</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>de Jong</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Bijlsma</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Wermenbol</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name><name><surname>Verweij-Uijterwaal</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name><name><surname>van der Avoort</surname><given-names>HG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Detection, typing, and subtyping of enteric adenoviruses 40 and 41 from fecal samples and observation of changing incidences of infections with these types and subtypes.</article-title><source>Journal of Clinical Microbiology</source><volume>31</volume><fpage>1562</fpage><lpage>1569</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8314997</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000503-Filho1"><label>11</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Filho</surname><given-names>EP</given-names></name><name><surname>da Costa Faria</surname><given-names>NR</given-names></name><name><surname>Fialho</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>de Assis</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Almeida</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Adenoviruses associated with acute gastroenteritis in hospitalized and community children up to 5 years old in Rio de Janeiro and Salvador, Brazil.</article-title><source>Journal of Medical Microbiology</source><volume>56</volume><fpage>313</fpage><lpage>319</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17314359</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000503-Grimwood1"><label>12</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-t